      "Claire Lomas, a charity campaigner, passed away at the age of 44 following an accident in Jordan on 22 August.",
      "Her family announced her death and requested privacy to grieve.",
      "Lomas became paralyzed from the chest down after a riding accident at the Osberton Horse Trials in 2007.",
      "She gained fame for completing the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days using a bionic suit.",
      "In 2012, she was honored to light the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square.",
      "In 2016, she participated in the Great North Run while pregnant, completing it in five days using her bionic suit.",
      "Lomas raised nearly £1 million for charity through various events across the UK."
    ]
  }
}
```

